  "term": "paramimia",
  "definition": "Paramimia is the inappropriate or incorrect use of gestures or other pantomimic forms of expression, especially in the context of aphasic disturbance. It refers to errors in nonverbal expressive signs rather than a complete loss of the ability to gesture.",
